# Files excluded from the Vercel deployment. The Vercel build is a static
# frontend (served from `frontend/`) plus one FastAPI serverless function
# (api/main.py, declared as the entrypoint in pyproject.toml) that serves
# /api/config (the GCS positions.json URL) and the other /api/* routes.
# Vercel reads its slim deps from pyproject.toml, NOT requirements.txt.
# Everything below is for local dev, the GCP Cloud Function, or the pipeline.

# Local virtualenv + caches
.venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__

# GCP infra + Cloud Function entry + heavy pipeline deps (managed by Terraform,
# not Vercel). main.py is the Cloud Function; requirements.txt carries its
# scipy/numpy/pandas/google-cloud-storage deps and is excluded so Vercel uses
# the slim pyproject.toml instead (no tree-shaking -> would blow the bundle).
# NOTE: the leading slash anchors these to the repo root. A bare "main.py"
# would also match api/main.py (gitignore patterns with no path separator
# match at any depth) and strip the FastAPI entrypoint from the build — which
# is exactly the "No FastAPI entrypoint found" error.
infra
/main.py
pipeline
/requirements.txt

# Generated data — the Vercel frontend reads positions.json from GCS, not the repo
data

# Misc
.github
plans
README.md
.gitignore
.vercelignore